---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Session from "../../components/Session.astro";
import Block from "../../components/Block.astro";
import Metronome from "../../components/Metronome.astro";
import { fretboardSVG } from "../../lib/fretboard.js";

const blocks = [
  { id: "warm", title: "Chromatic crawl", minutes: 5, bpm: 60, subdiv: 1 },
  { id: "mute", title: "Muting", minutes: 10, bpm: 60, subdiv: 1 },
  { id: "pick", title: "Picking", minutes: 10, bpm: 60, subdiv: 4 },
  { id: "song", title: "Song", minutes: 5 },
];

// String index: 0 = low E … 5 = high e.
const crawl = fretboardSVG({
  fretStart: 1, fretEnd: 4,
  dots: [1, 2, 3, 4].map((f) => ({ string: 0, fret: f, label: String(f) })),
  ariaLabel: "Chromatic crawl on the low E string, frets 1 to 4, one finger per fret",
});
const muteOne = fretboardSVG({
  fretStart: 3, fretEnd: 7,
  dots: [{ string: 3, fret: 5, root: true, label: "C" }],
  marks: [0, 1, 2, 4, 5].map((s) => ({ string: s })),
  ariaLabel: "One note, C on the G string fret 5. Every other string marked silent.",
});
const muteLine = fretboardSVG({
  fretStart: 3, fretEnd: 7,
  dots: [
    { string: 3, fret: 5, label: "1" }, { string: 3, fret: 7, label: "2" },
    { string: 2, fret: 5, label: "3" }, { string: 2, fret: 7, label: "4" },
  ],
  marks: [0, 1, 4, 5].map((s) => ({ string: s })),
  ariaLabel: "Four-note line: G string 5 and 7, D string 5 and 7",
});
const pickDots = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => ({ string: 5, fret: i + 1, label: String((i % 4) + 1) }));
const pickA = fretboardSVG({ fretStart: 1, fretEnd: 6, dots: pickDots.filter((d) => d.fret <= 6),
  ariaLabel: "Picking drill on the high e string, frets 1 to 6, fingers 1 2 3 4 then 1 2" });
const pickB = fretboardSVG({ fretStart: 7, fretEnd: 12, dots: pickDots.filter((d) => d.fret >= 7),
  ariaLabel: "Picking drill on the high e string, frets 7 to 12, fingers 3 4 then 1 2 3 4" });
---
<Layout title="Week 1 — Clean hands" description="Muting and metronome picking. Five sessions, 30 minutes each.">
  <Session blocks={blocks} />

  <h1>Week 1 — Clean hands</h1>
  <p class="muted small">21–27 Sep · phase: clean hands · nodes 5, 6, 17</p>
  <p>Five sessions, 30 minutes, timer per block. Sitting is fine this week. HX Stomp on the <strong>drive</strong> patch for every block: gain exposes what's ringing. Press <em>Start session</em> and the timer and metronome run each block for you.</p>

  <Block id="warm" title="Chromatic crawl" minutes={5} node={6}>
    <p>Low E, frets 1-2-3-4, one finger per fret (index 1, middle 2, ring 3, pinky 4). Then A string, up to high e, back down. One note per click. Strict down-up-down-up. Even volume on every note. Speed is not the goal.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={crawl} />
    <Metronome id="warm" bpm={60} subdiv={1} compact />
  </Block>

  <Block id="mute" title="Muting" minutes={10} node={5}>
    <p><strong>The test.</strong> Fret C on the G string, 5th fret. Pick it once. Let it ring four beats. Listen. Anything besides that C = fail.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={muteOne} />
    <p>Two fixes, both at once:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Picking hand.</strong> Heel of the palm rests on the low E and A strings, right at the bridge saddles. Not pressing. Touching.</li>
      <li><strong>Fretting hand.</strong> The index finger lies flat across the thinner strings (D, B, e), touching them, not pressing. The tip frets the note; the rest of the finger silences the neighbours.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Play the C. Four beats. Stop it with the palm. Ten times. Then D string 5th fret (G), ten. Then B string 5th fret (E), ten.</p>
    <p>Then a four-note line, each note two beats. Nothing bleeds. Ten times.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={muteLine} />
    <div class="note"><strong>Cramp check.</strong> Pinky or hand tenses: stop, shake it out, put the thumb behind the neck (not over the top), restart. Tension is the cramp, not weakness.</div>
    <Metronome id="mute" bpm={60} subdiv={1} compact />
  </Block>

  <Block id="pick" title="Picking" minutes={10} node={6}>
    <p>High e string only. Frets 1 to 12 and back, one finger per fret, shifting the hand every four (1-2-3-4, shift, 5-6-7-8, shift, 9-10-11-12). <strong>Four notes per click.</strong> Strict alternate picking. One pass = up and down.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={pickA} />
    <Fragment set:html={pickB} />
    <p><strong>Pass rule.</strong> A full pass with every note the same volume and no missed pick stroke. Three clean passes in a row: press +5. Any miss: stay. Write the BPM you end on in the log. Expect 60–70 all week. That is normal.</p>
    <p class="small muted">Days 3–5: same drill on the B string, then the G string. String crossing is not this week.</p>
    <Metronome id="pick" bpm={60} subdiv={4} />
  </Block>

  <Block id="song" title="Song" minutes={5} node={16}>
    <p>The hymn the team plays next Sunday. Once through on the drive patch, open chords, <strong>no stopping whatever happens</strong>. Listen for open strings ringing between chord changes. That is the muting problem inside a song.</p>
  </Block>

  <h2>Once this week: record</h2>
  <p>Day 4 or 5. Phone voice memo on the floor near the amp. Record the song block. Listen once, straight after. Note three things only: strings ringing between changes (yes/no), timing drifting (yes/no), one thing to change. Don't re-record.</p>

  <h2>Gate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Muting test: G-string C rings alone for four beats, drive patch, five times in a row.</li>
    <li>Picking: three clean passes at 60 BPM or more, four notes per click, high e.</li>
    <li>A recording exists.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Pass: week 2. Fail: repeat week 1. Repeating a week is the system working.</p>

  <h2>Log it</h2>
  <p>After each session, one line:</p>
  <p><code>guitar log: day N. picking ended at __ BPM on __ string. muting __/5 clean. song __ in __. felt __. improve __.</code></p>
  <p class="small muted">Also this week, no guitar needed: the eight hymns the team plays most, with keys, and the name of the patch pack.</p>

  <div class="lesson-nav">
    <a href="/drills/">All drills</a>
    <a href="/progress/">Progress &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</Layout>
